 <body>
    <h5> 
        2021-2022 Financial Year 
     </h5>
     <ul>
         <li> In partnership with the department of social development,Masimong has managed to establish a Community Nutrition Development Center (CNDC) whereby several services are being rendered to the commmunity.</li>
          <li>The department is assisting us in serving fifty(50) needycommunity members with nutricius food five days a week.</li>
          <li>Alberny bread is also donating hundred loves of breadper week for the poor.</li>
          <li>Masimong has partnered with meals on wheels in creating a food garden worked by 10 beneficiaries.</li>
          <li>This is an initiave to empower beneficiaries on agriculture for food security.</li>
          <li>In Safety and Security we have partnered with local SAPS and CPF in a fight against crime.</li>
          <li>SAPS has already trained sixteen volunteering Community Patrollers who patrol the area 24/7.</li>
          <li>We have adopted two netball teams under our name and plans are on the way to form a sports commitee.</li>
          <li>On 14/09/2021-16/09/2021 we embarked on a HIV/AIDS campaign.the awareness campaign was not financialy supported by a government department or any stakeholder and we managed to pay a visit to taxi ranks,shebeens,taverns and rural areas arround our area.</li>
           <li>On 25 September 2021 we hosted Heritage Day celebration whereby local and surrounding townships cultural groups displayed thier talents.Then Majhabeng's acting Mayor and sports,Arys and culture MMC gave speeches.</li>
           <li>House number 20 Cobalt in saaiplass belong to Mrs Lethopa was burnrd beyond repairs on the night of 21 October 2021.All her possessions were destroyed in that fire and she was left stranded untill the department of social development intervened by donating blankets, cloathing and food parcels to the familiy.</li>
           <li>On 09 November and 17 December 2021 the Health Department officials visited our center to vaccinate community members for COVID 19 and 130 community members got their first and second jabs.On 5 December 2022 we held Victim Empowerment Programme with assistance from Vriginia Victim Empowerment NPO,Department of Health,Department of Jusice,SAPS and Bophelo Youth.
           <li>On 28 and 31 December 2021 Albany Bakers donated one thousand loaves of bread and the bread was shared amoungst Masiming NPO beneficiaries and struggling community members.</li>
        </ul>
   <h5>
        2022-2023 Financial Year
   </h5>
       <ul>
        <li>From 04 may to 11 may 2022,we took an initiativr and visited 139 households in our community.The aim of the campaign was to establish how much does the community know about Masimong CNDC and which services have to be included in our programmes.</li>
        <li>On 20 may 2022,Mr Magoa borrowed Masimong Npo a 10000 liter JOJO tank.Although at Masomong NPO's custody,the JOJO tank remains MR Magoa's asset until decidedd otherwise by the two parties.</li>
        <li>On 14 September 2022,Masimong CNDC hosted SAPS "IMBIZO" whereby the community was given recent crime statisics.All crime "hot spots" were identified and the community complained about police response towards crime reports. </li>
        <li>On 24 September 2022 we celebrated Heritage Day whereby community members were invited.We had organised two netball and football teams which competed against each other.</li>
        <li>On 12 October 2022,Masimong NPO again offered venue to SAPS and Community Policing Forum(CPF) to elect a new CPF Committee for the branch.Masimong Chairperson was then elected as chair of the branch CPF and Masimong Dep.</li>
        <li>On 05 December 2022, we held Victim Empowerment Programme with assistance from Virginia Victim Empowerment NPO,department of health,Department of justice,SAPS and Bophelo Youth.</li>
        <li>From 06 March 2023 to 10 March 2023 we had  training  conducted by DSD officials.All our beneficiaries and interested community members were invited to take part.</li>
       </ul>

       

